A||||18||tgowens||FOCOA news!||||1||
Z||000000||tgowens||05-23-2001||01:21 AM||||I have recently heard that FOCOA (the club, not to be confused with FOCOA the business) is soon to be revitalized in many ways.<P>One of the issues it seems that many FOCOA members (myself included) have is the apparent lack of a timely magazine which is basically what the membership fee covered.....it is my understanding that the magazine <I>will</I> be produced and distributed to each member four times a year. It is also my understanding that there will be a National FOCOA web site which will include all chapter clubs (appx. 77 of them) within the eight FOCOA regions (which also include Canada) with contact names, web site addresses and email addresses for each of the clubs. My guess is that you could expect to see this by the early part of July.<P>One thing I would like to mention, there seems to be confusion as to who FOCOA is -- there are two separate entities - one is the club and the other is the business which sells Fiero parts and misc. Phil and Gloria are indeed still very active on the business side and will continue to do so. The club operations (as well as the club magazine) will be the responsibility of the Regional Directors and the Club officers.<P>I hope this may clear up any confusion there may be as to who is responsible for what part of FOCOA. <P>My guess is that you will hear more about this in the near future (especially if you are a member of a FOCOA chapter club) and/or a member of FOCOA (the club)......<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||05-23-2001||02:19 AM||||Sounds like a good plan!!  <P>Now who do we call/e-mail about not receiving the latest magazine issue?  Looks like everyone got theirs last week.  I just joined last fall, so my dues aren't up yet.<P>Will the magazine still be a "national" one or will be a "regional" one.<P><p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||05-23-2001||02:43 AM||||RossT, I am not sure about the magazine yet (I didn't get mine yet either!) - I do know there are changes being made to make FOCOA more responsive to the members. As for me, I am working on the web site end of it.......||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||05-23-2001||02:51 AM||||Thanks TG..  If the new FOCOA web site is anything like your other web site, it will be top notch!!<P>I am not trying to fuss to much about the magazine, but I really enjoy reading thru them.<BR>Last fall I purchased the entire set of backissues.  Took me a month to read thru them all.  That was fiero fun!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||05-23-2001||12:43 PM||||Thanks Ross! - I agree about the magazine and that will be addressed in the next couple of months.........I have a feeling you will see the magazines on time in the future.||||reg||1
